43	transaction	63	# transaction\n\n<img src="https://github.com/emberow/blog-image/blob/main/BlogImg/transaction.png?raw=true"/>\n\n1. During its lifecycle, a database transaction goes through multiple states. These states are called transaction states and are typically one of the following:\n2. Active states: It is the first state during the execution of a transaction. A transaction is active as long as its instructions (read or write operations) are performed.\n3. Partially committed: A change has been executed in this state, but the database has not yet committed the change on disk. In this state, data is stored in the memory buffer, and the buffer is not yet written to disk.\n4. Committed: In this state, all the transaction updates are permanently stored in the database. Therefore, it is not possible to rollback the transaction after this point.\n5. Failed: If a transaction fails or has been aborted in the active state or partially committed state, it enters into a failed state.\n6. Terminated state: This is the last and final transaction state after a committed or aborted state. This marks the end of the database transaction life cycle.\n\n## ACID\nComplying with ACID ensures that transaction events can be executed correctly\n\n### atomicity\nThe operations of the transaction are either all completed or not completed, and a rollback is triggered when it fails.\n\n### consistency\nThe data before and after success should comply with the constraints, otherwise the transaction will also be rolled back\n\n### isolation\nMultiple transactions can be executed concurrently without interfering with each other.\n\n### durability\nAfter the transaction modification is completed, the data is permanent and will not be lost even if system failures are repaired.\n\n\n## 隔離層級\n### Read Uncommitted\n允許讀取未提交的數據，可能會出現髒讀、幻讀、不可重複讀等問題。\n### Read Committed\n允許讀取已提交的數據，避免了髒讀的問題，但仍可能出現幻讀和不可重複讀。\n\n### Repeatable Read\n鎖定數據，確保在同一個 transaction 讀取同一個數據是相同的，不會受到其他 transation 影響。避免了髒讀和不可重複讀的問題，但仍可能出現幻讀。\n### Serializable\n強制將各個 transation 依序執行，避免了髒讀、不可重複讀和幻讀等問題，但性能較差。\n	t	2024-05-07 22:36:37.331+08
